# Edge platform spec

Read `00-beacon-shared.mdc`, then `docs/TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md` §6, §7, §9, §11 (Edge/Both tables), §12, §15, §16. This file adds what the design leaves open, the migration from the existing E1/E4 code, and the milestones.

## 1. Current state (already built, on `develop`)
- E1: Docker Postgres (host port 5433), Alembic `001_e1_initial`, staff PIN login, device pairing, QR payload, `/me`, `make seed`, tests.
- E4: `/ship/*` endpoints (overview, near-misses, wellbeing k-anon, deterministic brief, notices, fleet/medical alerts) + tests.
These were built for the old spec. **M0 migrates them**; reuse what fits (DB session, settings, logging, JWT utils, seed pattern, test fixtures, k-anon logic), replace the rest.

## 2. Runtime
```
docker compose up -d db                     # postgres+pgvector on :5433
ollama serve                                # native on the host (Metal/GPU); not in Docker on the demo Mac
uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8443 \
  --ssl-keyfile ../certs/beacon.ship.local-key.pem --ssl-certfile ../certs/beacon.ship.local.pem
python -m app.sync.worker                   # or run inside the API process as a lifespan task (DECISION: separate process is easier to see in the demo)
```
Settings (`BEACON_` prefix): `VESSEL_ID=v-0007`, `VESSEL_CODE=0007`, `VESSEL_NAME`, `VESSEL_SECRET`, `EDGE_URL=https://beacon.ship.local:8443`, `DATABASE_URL`, `JWT_SECRET`, `AI=fake|ollama`, `OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434`, `SHORE_URL`, `SHORE_API_KEY`, `LINK_OVERRIDE=auto|up|down`, `DATA_DIR=./data`, `WEB_DIST=../web/apps/crew/dist`, `ROSTER_FILE=../seed/crew_v-0007.json`.
Serve the built crew app from `WEB_DIST` at `/` (SPA fallback); API at `/api/v1`. Same origin, so no CORS.

## 3. M0: migrate to the contract and the POC schema
1. `pip install -e ../contract`; delete local payload duplicates; responses use `beacon_contract.edge_api` models (`response_model=`).
2. New Alembic revision `002_poc_schema` (demo data only, so drop old tables): every **Edge** and **Both** table in §11 (`vessels, crew, devices, tickets, ticket_media, ticket_actions, ticket_messages, learnings, learning_media, learning_acks, learning_stats, checkins, checkin_aggregates, anchor_cards, anchor_reactions, anchor_stats, welfare_requests, outbox, sync_state, inbox`) plus edge-only helpers: `pairing_codes(code, crew_id, expires_at, used_at)`, `drafts(draft_id, crew_id, status, transcript_original, original_language, fields jsonb, clarifying_question jsonb, confidence, created_at)`, `idempotency(key, route, crew_id, response jsonb)`, `rail_hits(rule_id, ship_date, count)`, `briefs(brief_date, payload jsonb, created_at)`, `fleet_alerts(alert_id, payload jsonb, received_at, read_at)`, `ticket_seq(vessel_id, last_seq)`. `checkins` has **no text column**. `tickets.embedding vector(768)`.
3. Auth per §5/§7: roster loaded from `ROSTER_FILE` by `make seed`; `POST /auth/pairing-codes` (Master) creates a code for a `crew_id`; `POST /auth/pair` sets the PIN (argon2) and returns a device token; `POST /auth/login` returns a 12 h session JWT `{sub: crew_id, role, vessel_id, device_id}`; 5 wrong PINs lock the device 15 min; `DELETE /auth/devices/{id}`. `make pair-master` prints a pairing code + QR (terminal QR via `qrcode`) for `c-0007-mst`.
4. Move the safety rails to `edge/app/safety/` (Sumit owns the logic; M0 only relocates `rails.py` and reads `edge/app/safety/rules/lexicon.json`). Remove all imports of `contracts/`. Delete `contracts/` at the end of M0.
5. Keep `GET /api/v1/health` as an alias of `/healthz` (returns `Healthz`).
6. Port tests; keep: k-anon (4 → hidden, 5 → visible), crew token → 403 on master routes, reporter identity never in master responses unless opted in.

## 4. API (§12) → contract models
All under `/api/v1`, Bearer session JWT except `pair`, `healthz`. Writes honour `Idempotency-Key`.

| Route | Request → Response |
|---|---|
| `POST /auth/pairing-codes` | `PairingCodeCreate` → `PairingCodeResponse` |
| `POST /auth/pair` | `PairRequest` → `PairResponse` |
| `POST /auth/login` | `LoginRequest` → `SessionResponse` |
| `GET /me`, `PUT /me/preferences` | → `MeResponse`; `PreferencesUpdate` |
| `POST /reports/drafts` (multipart audio?, photos[] ≤3, text?, language?) | → `DraftCreated` |
| `POST /reports/drafts/{id}/structure` | → `StructureResponse` |
| `POST /reports/drafts/{id}/answer` | `DraftAnswer` → `StructureResponse` |
| `POST /reports` | `ReportSubmit` → `CrewTicket` (emits `ticket.new` to master channel, writes outbox) |
| `GET /reports/mine` | → `list[CrewTicket]` |
| `GET/POST /tickets/{id}/messages` | `MessageCreate` → `MessageView` / `list[MessageView]` (crew: own tickets only) |
| `GET /master/tickets?onboard_status=&severity=` | → `list[MasterTicket]` (`reporter_name` only if `share_name_with_master`) |
| `POST /master/tickets/{id}/ack` | → `MasterTicket` |
| `POST /master/tickets/{id}/actions` | `TicketActionCreate` → `MasterTicket` |
| `GET /master/brief`, `POST /master/brief/regenerate` | → `MorningBrief` |
| `GET /master/learnings/stats` | → `list[LearningStatsView]` |
| `GET /master/welfare`, `POST /master/welfare/{id}/ack` | → `list[WelfareRequestView]` |
| `GET /media/{media_id}` | photo bytes (Master: any; crew: own tickets) |
| `POST /checkins` | `CheckinStart` → `CheckinTurnResponse` (quick completes here; 409 if done today) |
| `POST /checkins/{id}/turn` (json text or multipart audio) | `CheckinTurnRequest` → `CheckinTurnResponse` |
| `POST /checkins/{id}/welfare-request` | `WelfareRequestCreate` → 201 (emits `welfare.request`) |
| `GET /checkins/history?range=7d|30d|90d`, `DELETE /checkins/history` | → `MoodHistory` |
| `GET /anchor/today`, `GET /anchor?days=14&saved=`, `POST /anchor/{id}/react` | → `AnchorCardView`; `AnchorReact` |
| `GET /learnings`, `GET /learnings/{id}/media/{media_id}` (Range), `POST /learnings/{id}/ack` | → `list[LearningCard]`; `LearningAck` → `LearningAckResult` |
| `GET /inbox`, `POST /inbox/{id}/read` | → `list[InboxItem]` |
| `GET /events` | SSE (§5 below) |
| `GET /sync/status` | → `SyncStatus` |
| `POST /sync/now` (Master) | runs one cycle, returns `SyncStatus` |
| `POST /sync/override {mode: auto|up|down}` (Master) | demo link toggle → `SyncStatus` |
| `GET /healthz` | → `Healthz` |

Reports flow details:
- `drafts`: save photos (resize 1280 px, JPEG q70, strip EXIF) to `DATA_DIR/media/`; save audio to a temp file. `structure` calls `gateway.transcribe` + `gateway.structure_report`; run local dedup (`gateway.embed`, cosine > 0.85 within 7 days → `similar_open_ticket`). Audio file deleted on `POST /reports`.
- `POST /reports`: allocate `ticket_no` (`ticket_seq`), `onboard_status=NEW`, `shore_status=QUEUED_FOR_LINK`, store `reporter_crew_id`, compute embedding, write the ticket + outbox row **in one transaction**, emit `ticket.new`, inbox nothing.
- Master `ack`/`actions` update `onboard_status`, insert `ticket_actions`, write outbox rows, emit `ticket.updated` to master + reporter channel, add an inbox item for the reporter.

## 5. SSE hub (`app/events`)
- `GET /events` streams `beacon_contract.events.SseMessage.encode()`; channels from `beacon_contract.events` (`vessel:{id}:master`, `crew:{id}`, `vessel:{id}:all`). Subscribe by role from the JWT.
- Auth: `Authorization` header (web uses `@microsoft/fetch-event-source`) **or** `?access_token=` query param (EventSource fallback).
- In-memory `asyncio.Queue` per connection + a ring buffer of the last 200 events per channel to replay by `Last-Event-ID`. Heartbeat comment `: ping` every 15 s.
- Events: `ticket.new`, `ticket.updated`, `message.new`, `learning.new`, `sync.status`, `brief.updated`, `anchor.new`, `checkin.reminder`, `welfare.request`.

## 6. Outbox and sync worker (§13.1, §15.2)
- Outbox row per change: `event_id` (uuid7), `entity`, `op`, `entity_id`, `version`, `owned_fields` / `payload` built **only** from contract payload models (`TicketEdgeFields`, `TicketActionPayload`, `TicketMessagePayload`, `LearningStatsPayload`, `CheckinAggregatePayload` (only when n ≥ 5), `AnchorStatsPayload`), after `scrub_text` and `collapse_rank_band`. `reporter_ref = security.reporter_ref(VESSEL_SECRET, crew_id, ticket_id)`.
- Link probe: `GET {SHORE_URL}/api/v1/healthz` every 30 s, 3 s timeout, 2 successes → UP. `LINK_OVERRIDE` / `/sync/override` wins.
- Cycle when UP: push (severity 4–5 first, then oldest; ≤ 500 events / 256 KB gz; `SyncDelta` validated; signed with `security.sync_headers`) → mark acked rows → upload pending photos (`POST /sync/media/{ticket_media_id}`) → pull until `has_more=false`, apply each `PullChange.typed_payload()` → fetch learning media via `/sync/media-url/{id}` → emit `sync.status`. Record `last_push_bytes_gz` (shown in the Master view).
- Apply pull changes: `ticket.shore_status` → update ticket + reporter inbox + `ticket.updated`; `ticket_message` → resolve `reporter_ref` by recomputing for tickets on this vessel, insert message, inbox, `message.new`; `learning.published` → store, fetch media, then `learning.new` (urgent also to master); `learning.retracted`; `fleet_alert`; `rail_update` → write lexicon; `anchor.scheduled`; `brief_enrichment` → store, regenerate brief, `brief.updated`.
- Backoff 5 s → 5 min. A Postgres advisory lock prevents concurrent cycles.
- `edge/tools/mock_shore.py` (FastAPI :9090) implements `/healthz`, `/sync/push`, `/sync/pull` (serves `contract/generated/fixtures/sync.pull_response.json` once), `/sync/media/*`, `/sync/media-url/*` for local work until shore-api is live. `make mock-shore`.

## 7. AI gateway seam (Basil builds the interface + Fake; Sumit builds Ollama)
`edge/app/ai/gateway.py` defines a `Protocol` (signatures in `40-ai.mdc` §3) and `get_gateway()` choosing `FakeAIGateway` (returns `beacon_contract.fixtures` objects, 1 s delay) or `OllamaGateway` by `BEACON_AI`. All routes call only the gateway.

## 8. Milestones (P0 first; see docs/PLAN.md)
| ID | Scope | Done when |
|---|---|---|
| M0 | Contract + schema 002 + roster/PIN auth + `make pair-master` + rails relocated + `contracts/` removed | tests green; pair a browser via QR code and log in |
| M1 | Reports API with FakeAIGateway, media, dedup stub, idempotency | `curl` flow draft → structure → answer → submit returns contract models |
| M2 | Master board, ack, actions, SSE hub | a `ticket.new` arrives on `curl -N /events` within 1 s of submit |
| M3 | Messages + inbox | reply round-trip on the edge (crew ↔ master) |
| M4 | Outbox + sync worker + mock shore + `/sync/status|now|override` | link DOWN → pending grows; UP → pushed, `last_push_bytes_gz` ≈ 2 KB, pull applied |
| M5 | Learnings pull/media/feed/ack/stats | published learning from mock shore appears in `/learnings` with media |
| M6 (P1) | Check-in endpoints, welfare, mood history, anchor today/feed from seed pack, morning brief | quick check-in + 30-day history + today's card work |
| M7 | HTTPS serve + web dist + `scripts/demo_reset.sh` | phone loads `https://beacon.ship.local:8443` offline-capable |

## 9. Tests
Contract-model responses for every route; idempotent replays; transactional outbox (ticket and outbox row together or neither); no forbidden keys in any outbox row; `scrub_text` applied (roster names never in outbox); `checkin_aggregate` only when n ≥ 5; reporter_ref resolution for shore replies; crew can't read others' tickets/messages; SSE replay by Last-Event-ID; sync against respx-mocked shore (signature valid, duplicate acks, cursor advance, override DOWN sends nothing).
